  "title": "Kourovka problem 20.112 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let F be a hereditary saturated formation and let w∗ F denote the class of\nall finite groups G for which π(G) ⊆ π(F) and the normalizers of all Sylow subgroups\nof G are F-subnormal in G. It is known that w∗ F is a formation. Must w∗ F be\na saturated formation?                                  A. F. Vasil’ev, T. I. Vasil’eva",
